{"schemaVersion":2,"book":"JOB","chapter":35,"sourceModule":"original-languages-step","targetBible":"bsb","proposalMethod":"exact STEPBible English gloss match against fixed BSB text","targetTexts":{"1":"And Elihu went on to say:","2":"“Do you think this is just? You say, ‘I am more righteous than God.’","3":"For you ask, ‘What does it profit me, and what benefit do I gain apart from sin?’","4":"I will reply to you and to your friends as well.","5":"Look to the heavens and see; gaze at the clouds high above you.","6":"If you sin, what do you accomplish against Him? If you multiply your transgressions, what do you do to Him?","7":"If you are righteous, what do you give Him, or what does He receive from your hand?","8":"Your wickedness affects only a man like yourself, and your righteousness only a son of man.","9":"Men cry out under great oppression; they plead for relief from the arm of the mighty.","10":"But no one asks, ‘Where is God my Maker, who gives us songs in the night,","11":"who teaches us more than the beasts of the earth and makes us wiser than the birds of the air?’","12":"There they cry out, but He does not answer, because of the pride of evil men.","13":"Surely God does not listen to empty pleas, and the Almighty does not take note of it.","14":"How much less, then, when you say that you do not see Him, that your case is before Him and you must wait for Him,","15":"and further, that in His anger He has not punished or taken much notice of folly!","16":"So Job opens his mouth in vain and multiplies words without knowledge.”"},"targetSegments":{"1":[{"id":"JOB.35.1.s1","position":1,"text":"And","normalized":"and"},{"id":"JOB.35.1.s2","position":2,"text":"Elihu","normalized":"elihu"},{"id":"JOB.35.1.s3","position":3,"text":"went","normalized":"went"},{"id":"JOB.35.1.s4","position":4,"text":"on","normalized":"on"},{"id":"JOB.35.1.s5","position":5,"text":"to","normalized":"to"},{"id":"JOB.35.1.s6","position":6,"text":"say","normalized":"say"}],"2":[{"id":"